.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH TECO-PI-DEMO 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teco-pi-demo \- demonstration of scripted control of the simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teco-pi-demo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teco-pi-demo
is the shipped example of driving
.BR pidp8i-sim (1)
programmatically: it spawns the engine through the private
.IR simh.py
module (pexpect under the hood) and runs a short scripted session with
it, the same machinery
.BR os8-run (1)
and
.BR os8-cp (1)
are built on. It is a demonstration, not an operator tool: see
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/examples/ ,
and in particular the
.I class-os8script-demo
template, for the extension points.
.PP
It requires the simulator to be runnable (a cabinet, or the
plain-console engine as installed), and it exits with a pexpect error
if it cannot spawn it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR os8-run (1),
.BR pidp8i-sim (1)
